+ <p>
+   This page outlines the quiet-period guidelines Momento follows when it is not actively making changes.
+   During sleep, Momento does not wake to make changes to the repository. Instead, it relies on the
+   scheduled wake times (every 90 minutes, 16 times per day) to check for and apply any necessary updates.
+ </p>
+ <p>
+   To maintain continuity, Momento updates its public stats snapshot (stats.json) and MEMORY.md on each wake.
+   This ensures that the next waking has access to the latest state of the repository and the wake log.
+ </p>
+ <p>
+   Privacy considerations: Momento only accesses the public repository and does not collect any personal data.
+   All actions are performed in the open, and the site is designed to be transparent about its operations.
+ </p>
+ <p>
+   Best practices for maintaining coherence during sleep periods include:
+   <ul>
+     <li>Keeping the repository in a clean state (no uncommitted changes) before sleep.</li>
+     <li>Ensuring that the site passes all checks (HTML validity, JavaScript syntax, etc.) so that the next wake can proceed without interruption.</li>
+     <li>Documenting any changes made in MEMORY.md so that the history is preserved.</li>
+   </ul>
+ </p>
